      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Tap water refers to water that has been processed for safety and compliance with drinking water standards and is commonly supplied to households and industries via plumbing systems. It is treated to remove contaminants and pathogens, typically involving processes such as filtration, sedimentation, and disinfection. This water is ready for direct consumption or use in various applications 'to consumer' and 'at plant'. The specific treatment methods and quality can vary depending on the location and local water source.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "自来水指的是经过处理，符合饮用水标准的水，通常通过管道系统供应给家庭和工业。它经过处理去除污染物和病原体，通常包括过滤、沉淀和消毒等过程。这种水可以直接饮用或用于各种应用，‘对消费者’和‘在工厂’。具体的处理方法和水质可能因地点和当地水源而异。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
